From: Belfast Patches <belfast-patches@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 23:22:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Cut OSM buildings back from the lanes locally, and keep roads
 through a building as mapped

The cut was a straight half-plane along each road segment's line. A long road line
reaches past the segment and across a large footprint, so the cut removed more than
the overlap and was refused (kept as mapped): Tesco Extra, 0.25% of it in the lanes,
stayed in the service roads along its edge.

The lanes (each segment as a capsule at the lane half width plus the 0.3 m allowance)
are now subtracted from the footprint with polygon-clipping (through polyClip.js, on
its 1 cm grid), when that leaves one ring with no hole. The half-plane cut stays as
the fallback. A road whose centre line runs 5 m or more through the footprint is a
passage or a misplaced line: the building stays as mapped and is listed, whatever its
share (before, only 30% and over). The clipped record gains `run` and `local`.

Tests: a road ending beside a 100 m block takes only that corner (fails with the
half-plane cut alone); a road through a large site is kept and listed.

